  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "From 2004 to 2008 Meiji's Pokémon chocolate snacks came with Pokémon Card Game promos, one in each box or pack, sealed in a clear cellophane sleeve with a strip of silver paint and marked with a red Meiji logo in the bottom left corner: 97 cards in eight series. Meiji had made its own Pokémon cards for its chocolates since 1997, but these were its first for the card game. The first series, in February 2004, used Ken Sugimori's art and was numbered in the ADV-P promos (051 to 062). Four series followed in the PCG-P promos: from June 2004 with the relaunched Pokémon Card Choco Snack (005 to 016), in June 2005 (063 to 075), October 2005 (101 to 112) and June 2006 (134 to 145). The last three were in the DP-P promos: Pokémon Choco Snack vol. 6 in February 2007 (005 to 016), vol. 7 in July 2007 (034 to 045) and vol. 8, a light corn snack, in March 2008 (080 to 091). Many of the PCG-P arts also came on English cards, in POP Series packs and EX expansions.",
